      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\n### Rationale for the Consuming Span \u0026 Address Boundary Patterns\n\nIn traditional C++, iterating over buffers is done using `for` loops, an index `i`, and pointer arithmetic (`buffer.data() + i`). This is notorious for causing off-by-one errors, out-of-bounds memory accesses, and variable tracking fatigue.\n\nBy upgrading to the **Consuming Span** (for writes) and **Address Boundary** (for reads) patterns, we achieve the absolute floor for code complexity:\n\n1. **Single Source of Truth:** Instead of maintaining a base address *and* a loop index *and* a remaining counter, you just track what is left.\n2. **Eliminates Index Math:** `payload.first(take)` safely grabs bytes, and `payload.subspan(take)` safely shrinks the view. The compiler handles the pointer arithmetic.\n3. **Idiomatic C++20/23:** Mutating a `std::span` is practically free (it\u0027s just a pointer and a size increment). It replaces the need for `std::views::chunk` entirely while being more readable.\n\nHere are the exact steps to implement this across the four chunking loops in your code.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Update Flash Writing (`util/egis/flasher_logic.cc`)\n\nIn `ProgramFlashPayload`, replace the `for` loop with a `while` loop that consumes the `payload` span directly.\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, AppError\u003e ProgramFlashPayload(\n    BootromComm \u0026brom, uint32_t flash_offset,\n    std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e payload) {\n  \n  // ... [erase logic remains unchanged] ...\n\n  std::println(\"--- Writing Flash ---\");\n  const size_t total_size \u003d payload.size();\n  uint32_t current_addr \u003d flash_offset;\n\n  while (!payload.empty()) {\n    // 1. Determine size and slice the chunk in-line\n    size_t take \u003d std::min(BootromComm::kMaxFlashWriteSize, payload.size());\n    \n    // 2. Write the chunk\n    if (auto res \u003d brom.WriteFlash(current_addr, payload.first(take)); !res) {\n      std::println(stderr, \"\\n[HALT] Flash Write failed at address 0x{:X}: {}\",\n                   current_addr, ToString(res.error()));\n      return std::unexpected(AppError::kBootromError);\n    }\n\n    // 3. Advance hardware address and consume the span\n    current_addr +\u003d take;\n    payload \u003d payload.subspan(take);\n\n    // 4. Calculate progress using the remaining span size\n    size_t done \u003d total_size - payload.size();\n    std::print(\"\\rWriting Progress: {} / {} ({:.1f}%)\", done, total_size,\n               (static_cast\u003cfloat\u003e(done) / total_size * 100.0f));\n    std::fflush(stdout);\n  }\n\n  std::println(\"\\n[OK] Flash Full Binary Write successful\");\n  return {};\n}\n\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Update Command Parsing (`util/egis/flasher_logic.cc`)\n\nIn `ProgramRawCommandPayload`, remove the `done` offset counter entirely. The span itself will track our progress through the firmware file.\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, AppError\u003e ProgramRawCommandPayload(\n    UsbInterface \u0026boot_comm, std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e firmware) {\n  std::println(\"--- Flash RAW CMD Binary Flashing ---\");\n  const size_t total_size \u003d firmware.size();\n\n  while (!firmware.empty()) {\n    auto packet_size_res \u003d GetNextPacketSize(firmware);\n    size_t offset \u003d total_size - firmware.size(); // Only needed for error reporting\n\n    if (!packet_size_res || packet_size_res.value() \u003e firmware.size()) {\n      std::println(stderr, \"\\n[ERROR] Parse failed or truncated at offset 0x{:X}\", offset);\n      return std::unexpected(AppError::kParseError);\n    }\n\n    size_t take \u003d packet_size_res.value();\n    \n    // 1. Slice the exact packet\n    std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e packet \u003d firmware.first(take);\n    \n    // 2. Consume the span so the next iteration starts fresh\n    firmware \u003d firmware.subspan(take);\n\n    // 3. Send the sliced packet\n    if (auto res \u003d boot_comm.Send(packet); !res) {\n      // ... [Error handling logic unchanged] ...\n    }\n\n    // ... [Read response logic unchanged] ...\n\n    size_t done \u003d total_size - firmware.size();\n    std::print(\"\\rFlashing Progress: {} / {} ({:.1f}%)\", done, total_size,\n               (static_cast\u003cfloat\u003e(done) / total_size * 100.0f));\n    std::fflush(stdout);\n  }\n\n  std::println(\"\\n[OK] RAW CMD Flashing Finished\");\n  return {};\n}\n\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Update Flash Backup (`util/egis/bootrom.cc`)\n\nSwitch to the **Address Boundary** pattern. We drop the `remaining` counter and instead just loop until `flash_addr` hits `end_addr`.\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, BootromError\u003e BootromComm::BackupFlash(\n    std::string_view filename, uint32_t total_size) {\n  // ... [file opening logic remains unchanged] ...\n\n  std::println(\"--- Executing CMD_MEM_READ (0x20) ---\");\n\n  uint32_t flash_addr \u003d EgisBootrom::kFlashBaseAddr;\n  const uint32_t end_addr \u003d flash_addr + total_size;\n\n  while (flash_addr \u003c end_addr) {\n    uint32_t take \u003d std::min(kMaxFlashReadSize, end_addr - flash_addr);\n\n    EgisBootrom::MemReadCommand req{\n        .address \u003d ToLittleEndian(flash_addr),\n        .access_size \u003d EgisBootrom::AccessSize::kUint8, // Assuming enum refactor\n        .count \u003d ToLittleEndian(take)};\n\n    auto resp \u003d SendStruct(req, kFlashTimeout);\n    if (!resp.has_value()) {\n      std::println(stderr, \"\\n[HALT] Failed at address 0x{:x}\", flash_addr);\n      return std::unexpected(resp.error());\n    }\n\n    if (resp-\u003esize() \u003c take) {\n      std::println(stderr, \"\\n[WARN] Incomplete payload received\");\n      return std::unexpected(BootromError::kResponseTruncated);\n    }\n    outfile.write(reinterpret_cast\u003cconst char *\u003e(resp-\u003edata()), resp-\u003esize());\n\n    // Advance address\n    flash_addr +\u003d take;\n\n    uint32_t done \u003d total_size - (end_addr - flash_addr);\n    std::print(\"\\rBackup Progress: {} / {} ({:.1f}%)\", done,\n               total_size, (100.0 * done / total_size));\n    std::fflush(stdout);\n  }\n\n  outfile.close();\n  std::println(\"\\nFlash Backup Completed\");\n  return {};\n}\n\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Update Flash Reading (`util/egis/bootrom.cc`)\n\nApply the exact same Address Boundary pattern to `ReadFlash`.\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected\u003cstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e, BootromError\u003e BootromComm::ReadFlash(\n    uint32_t offset, uint32_t length) {\n  std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e buffer;\n  buffer.reserve(length);\n\n  uint32_t flash_addr \u003d EgisBootrom::kFlashBaseAddr + offset;\n  const uint32_t end_addr \u003d flash_addr + length;\n\n  while (flash_addr \u003c end_addr) {\n    uint32_t take \u003d std::min(kMaxFlashReadSize, end_addr - flash_addr);\n\n    EgisBootrom::MemReadCommand req{\n        .address \u003d ToLittleEndian(flash_addr),\n        .access_size \u003d EgisBootrom::AccessSize::kUint8, // Assuming enum refactor\n        .count \u003d ToLittleEndian(take)};\n\n    auto resp \u003d SendStruct(req, kFlashTimeout);\n\n    if (!resp.has_value()) {\n      std::println(stderr, \"[ERROR] read_flash failed at addr 0x{:x}: {}\",\n                   flash_addr, ToString(resp.error()));\n      return std::unexpected(resp.error());\n    }\n    if (resp-\u003esize() \u003c take) {\n      std::println(stderr, \"[ERROR] read_flash failed (size mismatch)\");\n      return std::unexpected(BootromError::kResponseTruncated);\n    }\n\n    buffer.insert(buffer.end(), resp-\u003ebegin(), resp-\u003eend());\n\n    // Advance address\n    flash_addr +\u003d take;\n  }\n  return buffer;\n}\n\n```",
